2. What is IOC (Inversion of Control)?
Answer

IOC means control of object creation is transferred from developer to Spring Container.
Without Spring
EmployeeService service =
      new EmployeeService();
With Spring
@Service
public class EmployeeService {
}
Spring creates object automatically.

Interview Line

IOC means Spring Container manages object creation instead of the programmer.

3. What is Dependency Injection (DI)?
Answer

Injecting one object into another object.
@Service
public class EmployeeService {
}
@RestController
public class EmployeeController {

    @Autowired
    EmployeeService service;
}
Spring injects EmployeeService into EmployeeController.
Types
Constructor Injection ✅ Recommended
Setter Injection
Field Injection

4. What is Bean?
Answer

An object managed by Spring Container is called a Bean.
@Service
public class EmployeeService {
}
`
Spring creates:
EmployeeService Bean

5. What is ApplicationContext?
Answer

ApplicationContext is Spring's IOC Container.

Responsibilities:

Create Beans
Inject Dependencies
Manage Bean Lifecycle

6. What is Spring Boot?
Answer

Spring Boot is built on top of Spring Framework that reduces configuration and speeds up development.

Features:

Auto Configuration
Embedded Tomcat
Starter Dependencies
Production Ready

7. Why Spring Boot?

Before Boot:
100+ lines configuration
With Boot:
spring-boot-starter-web
Everything configured automatically.

8. What is @SpringBootApplication?
Answer

Combination of:
@Configuration
@EnableAutoConfiguration
@ComponentScan
9. How Spring Boot Application Starts?
@SpringBootApplication
public class App {

   public static void main(String[] args) {
      SpringApplication.run(App.class,args);
   }
}

main()
  ↓
SpringApplication.run()
  ↓
Create IOC Container
  ↓
Scan Components
  ↓
Create Beans
  ↓
Inject Dependencies
  ↓
Start Embedded Tomcat
  ↓
Application Ready

